# The image build context is this module directory; the Dockerfile wants only
# the production bundle and nginx.conf. Everything else (src, Gradle build
# intermediates, webpack caches) stays out of the context — pruning here, not
# in the Dockerfile, keeps `docker build apps/web` from shipping megabytes of
# irrelevance to the daemon.
#
# The ladder shape is deliberate: re-including a deep path needs every parent
# directory un-pruned too (the daemon walks parents and honors last-match-
# wins), hence the include/exclude alternation down the tree.
*
!nginx.conf
!build/
build/**
!build/dist/
build/dist/*
!build/dist/wasmJs/
build/dist/wasmJs/*
!build/dist/wasmJs/productionExecutable/
